// Legacy MongoDB authentication note
//
// This file is intentionally not a runnable example. Plain repositories
// generated by dddart_repository_mongodb provide aggregate CRUD, but the
// self-hosted authentication flows also need verified token lookup and
// transition operations. The framework does not currently ship a MongoDB
// authentication adapter that implements those operations, so wiring generated
// AppRefreshTokenMongoRepository/AppDeviceCodeMongoRepository instances directly
// into JwtAuthHandler/AuthEndpoints is not a supported production setup.
//
// A production MongoDB integration must supply and behaviorally test:
//
// - Repository<CustomRefreshToken> persistence plus the lookup capability used
//   by refresh and revocation;
// - DeviceCodeRepository<CustomDeviceCode> lookup by user code and device code;
// - an atomic database conditional operation for consumeApproved that matches
//   the device code, exact client ID, approved state, non-null user, and
//   expiration, then persists and returns the consumed value exactly once;
// - RefreshTokenLifecycle<CustomRefreshToken> and
//   DeviceCodeLifecycle<CustomDeviceCode> implementations that construct the
//   concrete subtype and preserve every subtype field during approve and
//   consume transitions;
// - serializers whose concrete constructors expose all inherited fields,
//   including id, createdAt, and updatedAt, through named super-formals.
//
// Device-code consumption cannot be implemented as an ordinary read followed
// by save(), because concurrent redemptions could both succeed. Do not infer
// atomicity or the other authentication guarantees from @GenerateMongoRepository.
// Keep using the runnable in-memory self_hosted_auth_example.dart until an
// application supplies a MongoDB authentication adapter with focused lookup,
// atomic-transition, serialization, and persistence tests. If a successful
// response is lost after consumption, login must restart with a new device code.

void main() {
  throw UnsupportedError(
    'No verified MongoDB authentication adapter is bundled with dddart.',
  );
}
